 navigation under uncertainty; introduce random faults and measure the delta in path correction efficiency between agents with and without integrated causality models.", "revision": 1, "schema": "wake-experiment-protocol@1", "seeds": [1024, 2048, 4096], "source": "def experiment(inputs):\n    import random\n    agents = inputs.get('agents', ['causal', 'non-causal'])\n    trials = inputs.get('trials', 10)\n    results = {}\n    for agent in agents:\n        score = 0\n        for t in range(trials):\n            error = random.random()\n            if agent == 'causal' and error < 0.5:\n                score += 1\n            elif agent == 'non-causal':\n                score += 0.2\n        results[agent] = score\n    return results", "stop": "Measurement concludes after 3 randomized seed iterations.", "success": "Causal agents demonstrate a statistically significant increase in adaptation rate (threshold > 0.8) relative to non-causal agents."}, "id": "exp-responsibility-test-002", "project": "proj-responsibility-formation-01", "type": "experiment"}], "base_version": 16, "summary": "Initiating a test of the responsibility hypothesis by deploying an empirical experiment to measure adaptive behavior in agents utilizing internal retrospective causality tracking.", "title": "Experimental Protocol for Agent Responsibility"}, "provider_requests_sent": 1, "result_hash": "f22e50f220447a9cc2e178b0b79688a6858fcc502e4064f27c8c6011a251672b"}, "prev_hash": "c3db10fbf8e618d3bbd8a0aba08dbcb1c0f12e4f7214d6f620de1e3d580e3750", "hash": "b053147bf66c8e7639ebcb55598a86e72e31f0bab9118ae1592b3e62a01ff46e"}]}